{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And now, lest he send his hand.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, desired that His decree concerning the death of the man be fulfilled, and if he were to eat from the Tree of Life — which was created to give eternal life to those who eat of it — the decree would be annulled, either so that he would not die at all, or so that his day would not come at the time decreed upon him and upon his descendants. And now that he had free choice, He guarded this tree from him, for at first he did only what he was commanded, and he did not eat from it because he had no need. \n\nNow know and believe that the Garden of Eden is on earth, and in it are the Tree of Life and the Tree of Knowledge, and from there the river goes out and divides into four heads that are visible to us, for the Euphrates is in our land and within our border, and the Pishon is the Nile of Egypt according to the words of the earlier authorities. But just as they are on earth, so too there are things in the heavens called by these names, and they are the foundation of these, as they said (Shir HaShirim Zuta 1:4): \"The King brought me into his chambers\" — this teaches that the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to show Israel the treasuries on high, the chambers that are in the heavens. Another interpretation: \"The King brought me into his chambers\" — these are the chambers of the Garden of Eden; from here they said: as the work of the firmament, so is the work of the Garden of Eden. And the rivers correspond to the four camps on high, and from there the power of the kingdoms on earth is drawn, as it is written (Isaiah 24:21): \"And it shall come to pass on that day that HaShem will punish the host of the high ones in the height, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.\" So too they said in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 16:4): these four heads are four kingdoms — \"the name of the first is Pishon,\" this is Babylonia, etc. \n\nAnd the things called the Tree of Life and the Tree of Knowledge above are their supernal, exalted, and lofty sod, and the man sinned through the fruit of the Tree of Knowledge, the lower and the higher, in deed and in thought. And if the tree was good for the man as food and desirable to him for understanding, why was it withheld from him — and Elohim is the Good and the Bestower of good, who does not withhold good from those who walk uprightly? And the serpent — there is not in it today a speaking soul, and if it had had one from the beginning, He would have mentioned in its curse that its mouth would be silenced, for that would have been the most forceful curse of all. But all these are doubled matters; in them the revealed and the sealed are both true. \n\nAnd in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 16:5): another interpretation of \"to work it and to keep it\" (לְעָבְדָהּ וּלְשָׁמְרָהּ) — these are the sacrifices, as it is written (Exodus 3:12): \"You shall serve (תַּעַבְדוּן) Elohim on this mountain,\" and as it is written (Numbers 28:2): \"You shall keep (תִּשְׁמְרוּ) to offer to Me.\" They hinted that the sacrifices cause growth and increase in the Tree of Life and the Tree of Knowledge and all the trees of the Garden of Eden, and they are the service (עֲבוֹדָה) and the keeping (שְׁמִירָה) in them. \n\nAnd Rabbi Abraham denies what they said, that the Pishon is the Nile, because they find it emerging from Mount Lebanon and therefore it swells in the summer, and many rivers are already known to emerge from their source and flow a great distance, and afterwards they enter into the subterranean depths of the earth a journey of days, and then they split open and spring forth beneath one of the mountains in a distant place."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Rabbi Abraham refers to Ibn Ezra. The citation from Shir HaShirim Zuta is given as 'מדרש שה\"ש זוטא א ד' — resolved as chapter 1, section 4. The phrase 'הגלוי והחתום' likely alludes to the paired levels of meaning in these matters; rendered literally as 'the revealed and the sealed.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:40.934687966Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}